1
00:00:01,318 --> 00:00:05,988
Idea2Alpha turns a stock idea into conditions you can test, and prove wrong.

2
00:00:06,851 --> 00:00:13,872
On the Try it page, you write an idea the way you'd say it, and Translate with AI sends it to the Gemini model we evaluated.

3
00:00:13,882 --> 00:00:18,211
Here is one of our 30 test ideas: stocks that have been very strong lately.

4
00:00:18,221 --> 00:00:21,973
The page highlights the vague word. It has no number yet,

5
00:00:21,983 --> 00:00:25,914
so the translator asks what “very strong” means, instead of guessing.

6
00:00:25,924 --> 00:00:29,133
Pick a different answer, and the conditions change at once.

7
00:00:29,143 --> 00:00:35,962
Program checks confirm every factor and value, and the screening engine, not the AI, finds the matching stocks.

8
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:42,258
On 30 test ideas with signed answer keys, a direct prompt matched only 4.

9
00:00:42,268 --> 00:00:48,218
The full pipeline matched 24 and 26 in two identical runs, against a target of 25.

10
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:57,942
Backtests from 2019 to 2026 compare each strategy with 0050 and with 200 random portfolios.

11
00:00:57,952 --> 00:01:02,754
One popular combination beat only 30% of them: indistinguishable from luck.

12
00:01:04,362 --> 00:01:10,119
A bull, a bear and a judge debate from a numbered fact sheet, and a checker flags unsupported claims.

13
00:01:12,471 --> 00:01:18,409
The replay locks a rule before the outcome: of 8 signals, 5 held and 3 failed.

14
00:01:20,088 --> 00:01:22,717
You can also ask the AI about the project.

15
00:01:26,899 --> 00:01:29,852
It answers from a fact sheet built from our run records,

16
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:36,406
and it declines to pick stocks.

17
00:01:38,105 --> 00:01:41,008
Every page works in English and Traditional Chinese.

18
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:47,779
Idea2Alpha. Test your stock idea before you trust it.

